ology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T08:26:41Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T08:26:41Z","body":"Interesting, is the `TOOLS_ENABLED` check actually necessary? I thought compilers were smart enough to optimize out `if (false) {}` (as `is_editor_hint()` returns `false` for non-editor builds - but maybe compilers don't expand `Engine::get_singleton()->is_editor_hint()` to `false` during compilation?).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841209583/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2848423210","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105907#issuecomment-2848423210","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105907","id":2848423210,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6px30q","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-03T04:29:18Z","updated_at":"2025-05-03T04:29:18Z","body":"> Interesting, is the `TOOLS_ENABLED` check actually necessary? I thought compilers were smart enough to optimize out `if (false) {}` (as `is_editor_hint()` returns `false` for non-editor builds - but maybe compilers don't expand `Engine::get_singleton()->is_editor_hint()` to `false` during compilation?).\r\n\r\nAfter this PR, the size of linux release template is reduced by 31KB. Removing the `TOOLS_ENABLED` doesn't affect the size, so I believe they are still compiled out without `TOOLS_ENABLED`.\r\n\r\nNot sure if we should remove the `TOOLS_ENABLED`. I found most of the other `Engine::get_singleton()->is_editor_hint()` in the codebase are not surrounded by `TOOLS_ENABLED`, but there are also some exceptions.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2848423210/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2893136431","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105907#issuecomment-2893136431","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105907","id":2893136431,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sccIv","user":{"login